(TIM-01 - `Get current time into <name>.` obtains the current date/time
 as a `time` value and brings the name into being; `a time called <name>
 is current time.` is the same thing said the other way round.
 Also covers: TIM-02, TIM-03.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox TIM-01.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   the get form makes a time
   the declaration form makes a time
   the second reading is not older than the first
)
Get current time into now.
a time called later is current time.
If now's type is "Time (static)" then, print "the get form makes a time".
Otherwise, print "the get form makes a {now's type}".
If later's type is "Time (static)" then, print "the declaration form makes a time".
Otherwise, print "the declaration form makes a {later's type}".
If later's unix is greater than or equal to now's unix then, print "the second reading is not older than the first".
Otherwise, print "the second reading went backwards".
